// Adapter-only wrangler config — read EXCLUSIVELY by adapter-cloudflare via
// svelte.config.js `adapter({ config: 'wrangler.adapter.jsonc' })`.
//
// Why it exists: the adapter rimrafs and rewrites whatever `main` points at in
// the config it reads. The real wrangler.jsonc points `main` at our hand-written
// Worker entry (src/worker/index.ts), which must never be deleted by a build —
// so the adapter gets this config, whose `main` is the SvelteKit worker the
// adapter itself generates. Deploys and `wrangler dev` always use wrangler.jsonc.
{
	"main": ".svelte-kit/cloudflare/_worker.js",
	"assets": {
		"binding": "ASSETS",
		"directory": ".svelte-kit/cloudflare"
	}
}
